// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: CMSTP App Paths Registry Key Modification
// Sigma ID: b6d235fc-1d38-4b12-adbe-325f06728f37
// Status: stable | Level: high
// Author: Nik Seetharaman
// Date: 2018-07-16 | Modified: 2026-08-27
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218.003, G0069
// Tags: car.2019-04-001
// Description: Detects modifications to the CMSTP App Paths registry key. This may indicate abuse of Microsoft
//   Connection Manager Profile Installer (CMSTP) for arbitrary code execution or UAC bypass.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate CMSTP use (unlikely in modern enterprise environments)
// References:
//   - https://lolbas-project.github.io/lolbas/Binaries/Cmstp/
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20190720093911/http://www.endurant.io/cmstp/detecting-cmstp-enabled-code-execution-and-uac-bypass-with-sysmon/
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20190722224110/https://oddvar.moe/2017/08/15/research-on-cmstp-exe/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ed4273b30b6bba81f525a9ba136c2bcdb6d8ca95/rules/windows/registry/registry_event/registry_event_cmstp_execution_by_registry.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 1 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\App Paths\\cmmgr32\.exe.*$" and (not(((RegistryKey endswith "SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\App Paths\\cmmgr32.exe\\CmstpExtensionDll" and (RegistryValueData in~ ("C:\\Windows\\System32\\cmcfg32.dll", "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\cmcfg32.dll"))) or RegistryValueData =~ "(Empty)")))
